/*
  Localizable.strings (hu)
  AstroTool

  The V2 UI's Hungarian translation table. SwiftUI's `Text("literal")`,
  `Button`, `Label`, `Toggle`, `Picker`, `TableColumn`, `.help()`,
  `.accessibilityLabel()` and `.navigationTitle()` all resolve their
  `LocalizedStringKey` against `Bundle.main` -- the app target's bundle, not
  AstroUI's library bundle -- at render time. Putting this table here
  therefore localizes every one of those call sites in AstroUI with zero
  call-site changes. The key is always the exact English literal; a key
  with no entry here falls back to that literal, so English needs no file
  of its own.

  Keep this reproducible: `scripts/extract-localizable-strings.swift`
  extracts every literal that needs an entry (run it with `--missing` to
  see exactly what's outstanding), and
  `Tests/AstroUITests/LocalizationCoverageTests.swift` fails the build if a
  key is missing one -- except for the allowlist of brand/domain terms that
  intentionally stay in English (see that test file's `allowlist`: AstroTool,
  FWHM, OK).

  Glossary (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-15-localization.md): integration =
  integráció · frame = képkocka · light/dark/flat/bias and stack stay
  English · calibration = kalibráció · target = célpont · night = éjszaka ·
  session stays English · culmination = delelés · altitude = magasság ·
  surface brightness = felületi fényesség · quarantine = karantén · audit
  stays "audit" · usable = használható · excluded = kizárt · rejected =
  elvetett · framing = képkivágás · field of view = látómező · narrowband =
  keskenysáv · broadband = szélessáv · mono = monokróm. Buttons use the
  Hungarian macOS "-ás/-és" command-noun convention ("Mentés", "Mégse"),
  explanatory text is informal ("tegeződés").
*/

