// W5-2 finding 3 (owner pixel review): these two were keyed with a single
// `%`, but `PlanningView.swift`'s `Text("\(pct, format: ...)% of edge")` /
// "...% of short edge" both contain an INTERPOLATION, and a
// `LocalizedStringKey` doubles every literal `%` in a string that has any
// interpolation at all (verified with `dump()` on the actual SwiftUI type --
// see `scripts/extract-localizable-strings.swift`'s `assembleKey`), so the
// real runtime lookup key is `%@%% of edge`/`%@%% of short edge`, not
// `%@% of edge`/`%@% of short edge`. The old single-`%` entries never
// matched at runtime, so both columns silently stayed in English.
